description:
After zerus-6a2u.2 stores the Apple credentials: redeploy the website mirror's update_feed.py (older versions reject a stable or nightly release with a macOS asset), set the repository variable MACOS_CASKS_ENABLED=true and dispatch nightly.yml on main. Order and commands are in docs/macos-distribution.md.

Acceptance, none of which has run yet:
- the sign job signs with Developer ID, notarytool accepts the submission and the ticket is stapled;
- the verify job installs zerus@nightly from the tap in a clean runner, passes Gatekeeper (spctl) and library validation, and the bundled self-tests start WebEngine and Terminal automation in the signed app;
- brew style and brew audit pass for both casks in the tap;
- publish-nightly commits Casks/the Ruby recipe for the zerus@nightly cask to ufna/homebrew-zerus and the mirror accepts the asset;
- on a real Mac: brew install, brew upgrade, and switching zerus@nightly <-> zerus through the GUI's update command keep settings and running agents;
- the next owner-triggered stable release with macos_cask=true publishes Casks/zerus.rb.
If notarization rejects a binary, fix entitlements or signing in scripts/sign-macos.py and record the cause here.
